  "seoBody": "<section><span class=\"eyebrow\">Quickler in South Africa</span><p>Field firms in South Africa run inspections, checklists and certificates over WhatsApp, with no app to install, and you only pay for active users. A field worker answers on the phone they already carry, and the answers become a clean structured digital record on a manager dashboard. From spaza shop site checks to electrical compliance work and fleet walkrounds, the record is live, machine-readable and graded red, amber or green, with a PDF export available the moment a document is needed.</p></section><section><h2>A structured digital record, not a stack of paper certificates.</h2><p>Most field compliance in South Africa still ends in a paper pad, a photo dumped in a phone gallery, or a form typed up back at the office hours later. Quickler changes the output. As a field worker answers over WhatsApp, the work becomes a live record on a dashboard the office can see straight away.</p><ul><li>Every answer, photo and voice note lands against the right line item in real time</li><li>Each item is graded red, amber or green, so a manager sees faults at a glance</li><li>The record is machine-readable, so it can be searched, filtered and reported on</li><li>A PDF certificate exports from that same record when a client or regulator needs a document</li></ul><p>The dashboard is the product; the PDF is a convenience on top of it. That is the difference between a record you can manage a business from and a folder of scanned forms.</p><h2>Built for how South African field teams actually work.</h2><p>South Africa runs a large, spread-out field-services economy: electrical and solar installers, plumbing and HVAC crews, security and facilities firms, mining contractors, fleet operators, construction site teams and lone workers covering wide areas. WhatsApp is already the default way these teams communicate.</p><ul><li>Field workers use the WhatsApp account on their own phone, with nothing new to issue</li><li>No rugged tablets or kiosks to ship to remote sites, mines or farms</li><li>Text, voice note or photo all work, so a worker is never blocked by a form</li><li>One dashboard pulls every job back to a head office in Johannesburg, Cape Town, Durban or anywhere else</li></ul><p>Quickler is rooted in UK compliance work, but it is built to work anywhere WhatsApp does, and South African field firms fit that shape closely.</p><h2>Upload your form and Quickler builds the WhatsApp workflow.</h2><h3>Electrical, solar, plumbing, HVAC</h3><p>Whether it is an electrical compliance check, a solar install sign-off or a plumbing job sheet, upload the form your firm already uses and quickler turns it into a guided WhatsApp workflow with photos and ratings.</p><h3>Vehicle, equipment and site checks</h3><p>Daily fleet walkrounds, equipment inspections, facilities rounds and site safety checks all run the same way. The record builds itself as the worker replies, and faults surface on the dashboard immediately.</p><h3>Fire, security and lone-worker checks</h3><p>Fire safety rounds, security patrols and lone-worker check-ins fit a checklist or assessment workflow. Quickler is job-agnostic, so any inspection your team writes down can become a WhatsApp flow.</p><h2>Quickler for South African field firms.</h2><h3>What does my team need to install?</h3><p>Nothing. Field workers use the WhatsApp account already on their phone. There is no app to download, and dormant users are free, so you only pay for who actually works.</p><h3>What do I actually get out of it?</h3><p>A clean structured digital record on a manager dashboard, graded red, amber or green. You can export a PDF certificate from that record whenever a client or regulator needs a document.</p><h3>Can it run my own forms?</h3><p>Yes. Upload the inspection, checklist or compliance form your firm already uses and quickler builds it into a WhatsApp workflow. It is not tied to any one trade or certificate type.</p><h3>How do I get started?</h3><p>Start free at <a href=\"https://app.quickler.co/signup\">app.quickler.co/signup</a>, see how the product travels on the <a href=\"/pages/global-field-compliance.html\">works-anywhere page</a>, or <a href=\"/pages/help/index.html#contact-form-section\">get in touch</a> to talk through a workflow for your firm.</p></section>",
